public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String input = "Hello World!123";
        String result = convertToUpperCase(input);
        System.out.println(result);
    }

    public static String convertToUpperCase(String input) {
        if (input.isEmpty()) {
            return input;
        }

        char[] charArray = input.toCharArray();
        for (int i = 0; i < charArray.length; i++) {
            char c = charArray[i];
            if (Character.isLowerCase(c)) {
                charArray[i] = Character.toUpperCase(c);
            }
        }

        return new String(charArray);
    }
}
```

This implementation uses the `toCharArray()` method to convert the input string into a character array. Then, it iterates through each character in the array and checks if it is a lowercase letter using the `Character.isLowerCase()` method. If it is, the character is converted to uppercase using the `Character.toUpperCase()` method and stored back in the character array.

Finally, the modified character array is converted back to a string using the `String` constructor that accepts a character array as the argument. The resulting string is returned as the output.

The time complexity of this function is O(n), where n is the length of the input string. This is because the function iterates through each character in the input string once, resulting in a linear time complexity.

